  "decoded_text": "{\"obligations\": [{\"text\": \"Sketch the roughness scoring module, gravel_lens/roughness.py, at the level of signatures and docstrings; no need for the full math yet.\", \"source_ids\": [\"m01\"]}, {\"text\": \"Target Python 3.12 and use only the standard library plus numpy as dependencies.\", \"source_ids\": [\"m01\"]}, {\"text\": \"The Rumble Index is computed per non-overlapping 60 m window of route distance and reported on a 0-100 scale rounded to one decimal, where 100 is the roughest surface we've logged.\", \"source_ids\": [\"m01\"]}, {\"text\": \"Use snake_case everywhere for naming conventions.\", \"source_ids\": [\"m01\"]}, {\"text\": \"Every metric-producing function gets a compute_ prefix.\", \"source_ids\": [\"m01\"]}]}",
